00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.630
Yeah, right! I can't even
imagine a quiet Tokyo!

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.870
Watch out for RAPT, ya hear?

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:56.040
They're definitely after ya
after that crazy cop car stuff!

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:00.280
Attention, please!

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:07.060
Train 726 from Shin-Tokyo
to Dai-Osaka will be boarding shortly.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.990
Well, that's me! Stay in touch, now!

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.460
And send postcards, too!

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.410
She left...!

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:30.850
And I got her all this to eat
on the way back to Osaka...

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:37.850
We need drastic reform to prevent
this from ever happening again.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.020
An increase of RAPT mobile units,

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.690
detailed information
on potential new criminals,

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.960
the adoption of strict curfews...

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.170
"Mysterious Explosion at
Metro Government Building"

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.190
A lot of smoke is still in the air,

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.990
"Governor of Tokyo and 58
Cabinet Members Presumed Dead."
and rescue teams sent in may
suffer from secondary disasters.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.350
What do you mean?

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:27.510
Simply that you are no longer needed.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:33.220
We were told to put gathering
information on the glowing brains

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.460
and acquiring one
a priority over everything.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.330
Yes. As things stood,
it would have been easy enough

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:45.570
for some new organization to
step in and rise to power.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.310
So we chose to act in advance...

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.830
...but the situation has since changed.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:58.610
That was quite the fight
you put up with us.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.490
Don't tell me you're..

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:05.490
Yes. We have joined hands
with his organization.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.860
Bailan's future is now secured.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:11.900
Our name is ZERO.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.060
This world's beginning
and ending lies in our hands.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.740
Was this Laoban's decision?!

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.710
It was my decision as current
director of the organization.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.730
This was necessary to ensure
the organization's survival.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.150
<i>Amy was first</i>...

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.910
Who're you?!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.580
What the...?!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.260
"Bye-bye! - Morons! - Losers!"

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.820
"Bye-bye! - Morons! - Losers!"
--What in the...?!

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:20.920
Damn it...!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.050
<i>With her help, I continued
making a list of the other staff</i>.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.610
<i>What my plan needed was someone
who made the impossible possible</i>.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:52.500
<i>Someone who could take a job
with a 99% chance of failure</i>

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.520
<i>and make it succeed 100% of the time</i>.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.260
<i>And then I finally met her</i>.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.710
Let's see...

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:10.680
20,000 here, and 30,000 there...

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.720
Huh?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:15.620
Aw, man. It doesn't add up...

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.920
Did I miscount somewhere?

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.470
Jo!

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.310
We did it!

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.870
That makes a full 50,000!

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.580
What should we spend it on this time?!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:46.550
Come out!

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:51.690
That's some skill.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:57.690
Just one.. I mean, two.. people
wiping out a gang of 100 cyberoids...

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.660
Who are you?!

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:03.000
I'm here to buy that skill of yours.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.900
The skill of an angel from Hell.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.400
You're pretty sharp.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:28.790
I'm breaking your contracts,
so I'll pay you the penalty fees.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:33.730
In exchange, all your ties
with Bailan will be severed.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.300
What?! That makes no sense!

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.840
So you're disbanding the team?

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.870
Eh? Seriously?!

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.110
Yes. So get your things packed.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:48.780
Amy! Did you hear?! We're disbanding!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.310
So?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:57.220
Sei's the one who hired us,
so it's also her choice to fire us.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:04.390
But... it's been pretty fun,
so I am a little let down...

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:08.100
--Amy, you're..
--Sei.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.160
You don't need us anymore, do you?

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.440
No.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:21.400
I've asked a lot from you girls
in the past, but not anymore.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.620
I see...

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:28.210
You can't be serious...!

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:37.020
Kyohei-<i>kun</i>. Thanks for everything.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:42.630
I apologize for being sudden,
but your services are no longer needed.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:47.800
It's not much, but I've wired you
your pay with a little extra thrown in.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:52.110
Please continue devoting yourself
to your patissier studies

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.870
and forget about..

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.460
In accordance with the Special
International Cooperation Act,

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:11.060
I, Ricky Glenford, have been asked
to act as Tokyo's general governor.

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:16.630
Since the tragic accident involving
the former governor and 58 others,

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:19.740
Tokyo has been threatened by an unseen menace.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.540
As the situation stands,

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.980
maintaining proper administration
and stable peace will be difficult.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:29.050
The Japanese and American
governments have deemed

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:33.050
the international city of Tokyo
to be in a state of emergency

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:38.120
and appointed select members to
the Tokyo Reconstruction Committee.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:43.960
As its representative, I, Glenford,
will work my hardest with the citizens

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:49.400
to bring back the city's light and hope.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:54.460
The time for Tokyo's rebirth
has come. That time is now!

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.570
--He's totally cool!
--I ask for everyone's courage.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.280
--He's like a movie star!
--I ask for everyone's courage.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.540
I will use it to stamp out

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.510
--What the hell's he babblin' about?
--the evil from this town!

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:06.050
--He can't do nothin'.
--Also, the memorial for the distinguished
and honorable former governor

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:08.150
--As if Tokyo'd ever change.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:09.720
--We're living a pretty decent life.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.720
--We're living a pretty decent life.
--and 58 others are currently
under construction.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.220
--What's wrong with that?!

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:22.220
May their spirits watch us,
and this town, prosper for all time.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.910
"For your unwavering sense of
loyalty and duty. Rest in peace."

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.680
Here goes!

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:21.330
We had a blast again today!
That makes six days now!

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:22.620
Seven.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.960
--Today is the seventh day.
--Is it really?

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.770
Jo... Don't tell me you're
bored hanging out with me?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.140
Not really...

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:37.410
Come on!

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.110
We hardly get time or money like this!

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.680
Don't you wanna do anything?!

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:47.410
Not really. I'll just do whatever you want.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.260
Still...!

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.780
What am I supposed to do?

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:04.740
Leo-<i>chin</i>!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.600
How's work?

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:11.000
You got a buttload
for your broken contract!

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:15.270
You should be in a hotel
suite taking it easy.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:19.780
I just can't calm down in hotels...

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.780
That doesn't mean you
can come bug me, though!

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.780
I can't work when there's people around.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.890
Anyway, let's go somewhere!
You got nothing else to do!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:37.890
Ha! Adults actually have to
work and eat right, you know!

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:44.680
Hello? Yeah, it's me.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:49.950
Leo-<i>han</i>?! Why haven't you
called? I've been worried!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.980
I heard the moron governor
died in an explosion

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:56.850
and that Glenford's been
bossin' Tokyo in his place.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.910
Talk about insanity!

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:01.420
Takane! What's up!

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:06.360
Huh? Was that Meg? What's <i>she</i> doing there?!

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.270
Not just me! Jo's here, too!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:12.240
Alright, Leo-<i>han</i>! Explain yourself!

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.070
--No, they just showed up and..
--Ditch the phone!

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:18.440
--Let's have more fun, Leo-<i>chin</i>!
--What?!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.100
You idiot! I told you, I'm working!

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.380
"Idiot?!"

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.380
No, no! I didn't mean you!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:30.220
--So you meant me?! How mean!
--Damn it! Knock it off!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.650
<i>Ugh!</i>

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:43.230
<i>And they called me over everyday
with no regard to my own situation</i>...

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:49.260
<i>But it is her. If she
says it's over, it's over</i>.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.280
What's the deal? You seem down.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:58.580
Anyway, check this out!

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.420
"Underworld News -- I Saw a Monster
in the Tokyo Subway System!"
All the subways in Tokyo
are in a panic over these rumors!

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.250
"Subway monster?"

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:11.930
People've seen a skeleton monster
thing running alongside the train!

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.870
RAPT is supposedly
hunting it down in secret.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.770
Could be related to that big explosion...

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.870
Whoops! See ya tomorrow!

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:25.900
Yeah...

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:37.950
Life form detected 70 meters
ahead at 3 o'clock.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:41.720
--Target moving at high velocity.
--Prepare to intercept!

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:50.830
What the...?!

00:14:59.180 --> 00:14:59.940
Fire!

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.650
You're certain?

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:12.860
Yes. I can only assume that
the shock from his death

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:16.260
caused his Third Neuron
implants to activate.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.830
What a dim-witted man.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.560
Little did he know he was
a test subject himself.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:28.940
Look at that. He's so
unsightly he deserves pity.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:33.170
This is the final stop for
the man who once ruled Tokyo!

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:37.980
The network is down all
along the path he's taken.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:41.880
If this keeps up, all of Tokyo's
municipal functions could be paralyzed.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:49.890
He gives us trouble even after being
dismissed for inadequate results.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:56.800
But taking on a good-for-nothing
watchdog would be bland.

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:02.300
Let us bring in a
monster-extermination specialist...

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:11.640
I'm so bored! Come on, let's go somewhere!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.320
Ugh!

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:21.590
Guess I'll go eat all by myself!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.890
Bah!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.110
I thought our contract was up.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:46.550
Yes. But this is a job only you can do.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.490
--Are we using Django?
--Yes. The enemy is..

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:53.390
Doesn't matter! I was just getting bored!

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.960
I'd like your help too, Jinno-<i>san</i>.

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:59.450
That's only natural if you're using Django.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:04.600
Huh?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:09.570
Did everyone leave?

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.170
Sheesh...!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:15.240
J-Jo?

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.580
Oxygen level down to 20%.

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:25.650
Target moving northeast at 15 kph.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.020
System functioning normally.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.690
Reducing oxygen level in sealed area.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:47.710
The plan is working. The target
is definitely heading this way.

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:52.180
I know you're only
following orders from above,

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:56.550
but I hope you're not going to turn
tail and run when the time comes.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:18:02.960
It's true that Bailan dispatched
me here with orders to assist you,

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:07.860
but that's no ordinary mercenary
waiting for the enemy there.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:13.200
Underestimate her and everyone
here... will see Hell!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.640
Emergency message from HQ!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:18.980
Understood!

00:18:18.980 --> 00:18:25.570
We'll drive him out as arranged!
The rest is up to you!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.120
--Jo.
--What is it, Sei?

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:43.630
As I mentioned earlier, this job
is to assist in a RAPT mission.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:50.530
I can't give any details, but I
had no choice but to accept it.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:54.680
That's fine. I don't really care.

00:18:54.680 --> 00:19:00.080
I only accepted it because
it was your request. That's all.

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:13.730
It's coming! At intense speed!

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.010
There it is!

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.650
It's huge!

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:45.350
Alright, freak! Let's go!

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.870
<i>Impressive, Jo</i>...

00:20:55.870 --> 00:21:00.640
<i>Your combat skills improve each
time you encounter a powerful enemy</i>.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:02.540
<i>So much it's frightening</i>...

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:10.540
Good work. Now I must ask
that you come with us.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.550
You and that mercenary...!

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:21.890
Sei! Stay alive!

00:21:56.590 --> 00:22:04.260
I remained motionless within the crowd

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:11.900
Not even the voice of my
tears carried on this street

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:19.610
as my feelings of lonesomeness joined it

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:28.990
In truth, everyone wants
to smile with each other,

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:35.530
yet they get hurt
when they can't do it very well

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:44.540
But someone will always
be there to watch,

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:51.470
so let's walk together
beneath this sky

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:17.300
<i>When did it take place? Who was behind it?</i>

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:21.570
<i>An old fight bursts into
an intense conflagration...</i>

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:25.700
<i>On the next Burst Angel:</i>
"Beloved Devil"
